  "description": "Reason about when a Flow is inside the caller's transaction vs starts its own. Pick Before-Save vs After-Save vs Async Path vs Pause + Resume when transaction boundaries matter. Covers governor-limit sharing, DML sequencing, recoverability, and the limits that reset when a new transaction starts. NOT for choosing Flow vs Apex (use admin/process-automation-selection) or record-triggered design \u2014 use flow/record-triggered-flow-patterns.",
  "file_location": "skills/flow/flow-transactional-boundaries",
  "id": "flow/flow-transactional-boundaries",
  "inputs": [
    "Flow entry point (record-triggered, screen, autolaunched, scheduled, orchestration)",
    "Work the flow must perform (DML, callouts, loops, time delay)",
    "Upstream caller context (DML trigger, Apex, UI, scheduler, Platform Event)"
  ],
  "name": "flow-transactional-boundaries",
